  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DSH Conversation Navigator",
      "text": "A client-only DSH Web plugin that adds a turn navigation rail to the left of the chat flow.\n\nEach marker corresponds to one user message and the following assistant work, which is DSH's complete conversation-turn boundary. The marker positions follow the rendered message locations. The marker intersecting the viewport center is highlighted. Hovering a marker shows the beginning of the user's message, and clicking it smoothly scrolls to that turn."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "From this checkout:\n\n```powershell\ndsh plugin --profile web add D:\\dsh-locateHistory\n```\n\nRestart the existing DSH Web process, then refresh `http://127.0.0.1:3080`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Notes",
      "text": "- The rail is hidden below `900px` viewport width to avoid overlapping the mobile chat layout.\n- It reads stable attributes already emitted by DSH's chat flow: `data-conversation-scroll`, `data-chat-flow-kind`, and `data-chat-anchor-key`.\n- A new user message without a completed assistant response is still shown as the current open turn."
    }
  ],
